    "result_text": "The full suite is green (34 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier by following the existing `namesakeCount` create-time-signal pattern, since the tier is served on `GET` (a reload from the DB) and so must be derived from persisted state.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema** \u2014 added a `household_size INTEGER` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n\n3. **New function `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 counts the owner's household members after this create: stored owners sharing the same `householdId` plus the new owner itself (`+1`, since it isn't saved yet). An owner not in a shared household (`householdId == null`) gets size 1. It runs after `AssignHousehold` (so the `householdId` is set and existing members are backfilled) and before `save`.\n\n4. **POST pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 wired `assignHouseholdSize` between `assignHousehold` and `assignCustomerCode`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling through to the unchanged `SILVER`/`BRONZE` rule.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description.\n\nBackward compatibility holds: pre-existing/seed owners have a null `householdSize`, so they fall through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic exactly as before.",
